<p>The <strong>under desk elliptical vs walking pad</strong> decision comes down to one question: do you want to keep sitting while you move, or do you want to stand up and walk? A seated elliptical slides under the desk you already have and keeps your legs moving while you type. A walking pad is a slim, motorized treadmill deck that sits under a standing desk so you can walk at a slow pace while you work.</p>
<p>Both add movement to a desk-bound day, but they suit different people. The walking pad wins on calories and step counts. The elliptical wins on cost, noise, desk compatibility and keeping your focus on work. Below is the full head-to-head, then a short checklist that tells you which one to buy.</p>

<h2>Under Desk Elliptical vs Walking Pad at a Glance</h2>
<p>Here is how the two categories compare on the factors that matter most once the box is open and the novelty wears off.</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Under desk elliptical</th><th>Walking pad</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
