<h2>Under Desk Elliptical or Walking Pad: Which Should You Buy?</h2>
<p>Run through these questions in order. The first one that clearly applies to you usually decides it.</p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Do you have a standing desk?</strong> No, and you do not want one: buy an under desk elliptical.</li>
<li><strong>Is most of your day calls, focused typing or detailed mouse work?</strong> Choose the seated elliptical. You will use it for more hours.</li>
<li><strong>Do you share a space or live above someone?</strong> The quieter elliptical is the safer choice.</li>
<li><strong>Do you track steps and want them to count?</strong> A walking pad gives you real, tracker-friendly steps.</li>
<li><strong>Is your main goal burning more calories?</strong> A walking pad edges ahead per hour, as long as you will actually stand on it for an hour or more a day.</li>
<li><strong>Do you have balance issues, joint pain or limited stamina?</strong> Start with a seated elliptical.</li>
</ol>
<p>If you are still split, take our <a href="/tools/which-under-desk-elliptical-quiz/">60-second quiz</a>. It factors in desk height, noise and your goals.</p>
<h3>The case for owning both</h3>
<p>Plenty of remote workers end up with one of each. They walk during meetings with the camera off and pedal seated through deep-work blocks. If that sounds like you, start with the cheaper elliptical, see how much you use it, and add a walking pad later. Also see <a href="/under-desk-elliptical-benefits/">the main under desk elliptical benefits</a>, and our guide to <a href="/is-under-desk-elliptical-as-good-as-walking/">whether an under desk elliptical is as good as walking</a> breaks down how the two compare for health.</p>

<h2>Our Verdict on the Under Desk Elliptical vs Walking Pad</h2>
<p>For most people working at a regular desk, the under desk elliptical vs walking pad question has a simple answer: the elliptical is the easier habit to keep. It is cheaper, quieter, needs no new furniture and does not interfere with your work, so it gets used for more hours. The [[amazon:cubii-jr2|Cubii JR2]] is our first choice.</p>
<p>If you already own a standing desk, you want steps on your tracker and your work is mostly calls and email, a walking pad gives you a bit more burn per hour. The [[amazon:walkingpad-c2|WalkingPad C2]] is a good place to start. Before you buy either, check how <a href="/how-to-use-under-desk-elliptical/">to set up and use an under desk elliptical</a> or compare it with a full <a href="/under-desk-elliptical-vs-treadmill/">under desk treadmill</a>.</p>
